  "database": "rschema_0328",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0328 database is designed to manage and store data related to online surveys. The Administrator table contains information about the administrators of the system, including their account names, unique IDs, names, passwords, and phone numbers. Each administrator is uniquely identified by their Administrator_ID, which is the primary key. The Survey table stores details about the surveys themselves, including their titles, descriptions, start and end times, access restrictions, and logos. Each survey has a unique ID, which is the primary key. The Question table contains the questions within each survey, along with their titles, descriptions, display styles, evaluation scores, and validation types. Questions are linked to their respective surveys through the Survey_ID foreign key, which references the Survey table. The Option table stores the possible choices for multiple-choice questions, with each option having a unique ID, display order, and content. Options are linked to their parent questions through the Question_ID foreign key, which references the Question table. The Text_answer_record table stores the text-based answers provided by respondents, including the answer content, question ID, respondent information, and submission time. The Choice_answer_record table stores the multiple-choice answers provided by respondents, including the answer type, option ID, respondent information, and submission time. Both the Text_answer_record and Choice_answer_record tables reference the Question table through the Question_ID foreign key, which ensures that each answer is linked to its corresponding question.",
  "gold_question": "This is an online survey system. For administrator management, the system maintains administrator information including name, phone number, account, and password. Administrators can register, log in to the system, create, edit, delete surveys, and view survey statistics. For survey management, the system supports creating surveys, setting survey title, description, access restrictions, start and end times, access rules (public or password-protected), survey status (created, in progress, ended), survey logo URL and background image URL, anonymity settings, etc. Surveys can be associated with multiple questions. For question management, the system supports creating different types of questions (single choice, multiple choice, text, text area), setting question title, description, required status, validation type, display order, display style, evaluation status, evaluation score, etc. Questions can be associated with multiple options. For option management, the system supports creating options for questions, setting option content, display order, correct answer status, etc. Options can be single or multiple choice type. For answer recording, the system records users' answers to single or multiple choice questions, including option ID, answer type, submission time, respondent information, and also records users' answers to text questions, including question ID, answer content, submission time, and respondent information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0328.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0328\nCREATE TABLE `administrator` (\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`administrator_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `survey` (\n  `survey_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `access_restriction` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `logo` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`survey_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `question` (\n  `question_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `survey_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `display_style` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `evaluation_score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `validation_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`question_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `question_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`survey_id`) REFERENCES `survey` (`survey_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `option` (\n  `option_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `question_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `display_order` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`option_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `option_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`question_id`) REFERENCES `question` (`question_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `text_answer_record` (\n  `text_answer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `question_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `respondent_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `answer_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `submission_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`text_answer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `text_answer_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`question_id`) REFERENCES `question` (`question_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `choice_answer_record` (\n  `choice_answer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `question_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `option_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `respondent_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `answer_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `submission_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`choice_answer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `choice_answer_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`question_id`) REFERENCES `question` (`question_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `choice_answer_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`option_id`) REFERENCES `option` (`option_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
